            <ArticleTitle>Chirality sensing with stereodynamic copper(I) complexes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>663-669</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/chir.22765</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three Cu(I) complexes derived from stereodynamic diphosphine ligands were synthesized and used for chirality sensing. The coordination of diamines and amino acids to these complexes generates distinct circular dichroism signals. The chiroptical sensor response allows determination of the absolute configuration and the enantiomeric excess of the analyte at low concentrations. This method is operationally simple, fast, and attractive for high-throughput sensing applications.</AbstractText>
